Question Title: API-Service Directory Workflow

Question Link: https://my.newtonschool.co/playground/code/5ypni48t3pzs

Solution:
cd api-service
git init
git add README.md
git commit -m "Add documentation"
git add server.js routes.js package.json
git commit -m "Add server files"
git status
git log

Approach:
1. Moved into the api-service directory and initialized a Git repository with git init.
2. Staged only README.md and committed it with the message "Add documentation".
3. Staged server.js, routes.js and package.json by name and committed them with the message "Add server files".
4. Did not use git add . so draft.md and .env were never staged.
5. Ran git status to confirm draft.md and .env are still untracked, and git log to confirm both commits.